---
import Layout from '@layouts/Layout.astro';
const title = "Shenzhen Travel Guide: Tech Hub Next to Hong Kong";
const description = "Visit Shenzhen — China's tech capital, gateway to Hong Kong, mountain-and-sea outdoor adventures, and a modern city built in just 40 years.";
---

<Layout title={title} description={description} lang="en">
  <article class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-6 py-12">
    <header class="mb-12">
      <p class="text-sm text-gray-500 mb-3">🏙️ Shenzhen</p>
      <h1 class="text-4xl font-extrabold text-gray-900 mb-4 leading-tight">Shenzhen Travel Guide: Tech Hub Next to Hong Kong</h1>
      <p class="text-xl text-gray-600 mb-6">Visit Shenzhen — China's tech capital, gateway to Hong Kong, mountain-and-sea outdoor adventures, and a modern city built in just 40 years.</p>
      <div class="flex items-center gap-4 text-sm text-gray-500"><span>📅 Last updated: June 2026</span><span>⏱️ 8 min read</span></div>
    </header>

    <div class="bg-gradient-to-r from-cyan-50 to-blue-50 border-l-4 border-cyan-500 rounded-r-2xl p-8 mb-12 not-prose">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-cyan-900 mb-4">⚡ Quick Answer</h2>
      <p class="text-lg text-cyan-800 leading-relaxed">Shenzhen is <strong>China's Silicon Valley</strong> — a city that grew from a fishing village to a 20-million-person megacity in just four decades. It's ultramodern, green, and the easiest place to cross into Hong Kong. If you're into tech, seafood, outdoor activities, or want to visit both mainland China and Hong Kong in one trip, Shenzhen is your city.</p>
    </div>

    <nav class="bg-gray-50 rounded-2xl p-8 mb-12 not-prose">
      <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-gray-900 mb-4">📋 In This Guide</h3>
      <ul class="space-y-3">
        <li><a href="#why-visit" class="text-blue-600 hover:underline">🤖 Why Visit Shenzhen?</a></li>
        <li><a href="#how-many-days" class="text-blue-600 hover:underline">📅 How Many Days Do You Need?</a></li>
        <li><a href="#attractions" class="text-blue-600 hover:underline">🎯 Top Attractions</a></li>
        <li><a href="#getting-around" class="text-blue-600 hover:underline">🚇 Getting Around</a></li>
        <li><a href="#where-to-stay" class="text-blue-600 hover:underline">🏨 Where to Stay</a></li>
        <li><a href="#what-to-eat" class="text-blue-600 hover:underline">🍜 What to Eat</a></li>
      </ul>
    </nav>

    <h2 id="why-visit" class="text-3xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-6 mt-12">🤖 Why Visit Shenzhen?</h2>
    <p class="text-lg leading-relaxed text-gray-700 mb-12">Shenzhen is living proof of China's economic miracle. It's home to tech giants (Huawei, Tencent, DJI), futuristic architecture, and some of the best seafood in the country. It's also the main land border crossing to Hong Kong — you can be in Kowloon in under an hour by metro. For travelers who want to experience modern China at its most dynamic, Shenzhen delivers. Plus, the city's "Mountains-Sea-City" (山海连城) initiative has created stunning coastal cycling routes and mountain hikes that make it a hidden gem for outdoor lovers.</p>

    <h2 id="how-many-days" class="text-3xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-6 mt-12">📅 How Many Days Do You Need?</h2>
    <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-2 text-lg text-gray-700 mb-4">
      <li><strong>2–3 days (standard):</strong> City sights, seafood, and a Hong Kong day trip</li>
      <li><strong>4–5 days (comfortable):</strong> Add Window of the World, Shenzhen Bay, and OCT Loft art district</li>
      <li><strong>5+ days (extended):</strong> Combine with Hong Kong for 2–3 days, or take a ferry to Macau</li>
    </ul>
    <p class="text-lg text-gray-700 mb-2"><strong>For sports & outdoor lovers:</strong> Add an extra day for the "Mountains-Sea-City" trail — cycle from Taiziwan to Shenzhen Bay along the coast (2–3 hours), or hike Qiniangshan on the Dapeng Peninsula for mountain-meets-ocean views (half day).</p>
    <p class="text-lg text-gray-700 mb-4">If you're staying longer, consider a side trip to Hong Kong. The high-speed rail or metro connection to Hong Kong takes under an hour.</p>
    <div class="bg-blue-50 border-l-4 border-blue-400 p-4 mb-12 rounded-r-lg text-blue-800 text-sm">
      🌏 <strong>Note for travelers using the 240-hour visa-free transit policy:</strong> Hong Kong (香港, China) is considered a separate customs territory, so crossing into Hong Kong satisfies the requirement of departing mainland China to a "third country or region." If your itinerary starts in Shenzhen, you can exit through Hong Kong without needing a separate visa for that leg of the trip. See: <a href="/en/visa/visa/transit-240/" class="text-blue-600 underline">China 240-Hour Visa-Free Transit Explained</a>.
    </div>

    <!-- ==================== ATTRACTIONS ==================== -->
    <h2 id="attractions" class="text-3xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-6 mt-12">🎯 Top Attractions</h2>

    <!-- OCT Loft (short text → keep 2-col grid) -->
    <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-8 items-start bg-white border border-gray-200 rounded-2xl p-6 mb-6">
      <div class="w-full rounded-2xl overflow-hidden">
        <img src="/images/shenzhen/oct-loft.png" alt="OCT Loft creative arts district with street art and galleries in Shenzhen" class="w-full h-auto object-cover" loading="lazy" />
      </div>
      <div>
        <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">OCT Loft (华侨城创意文化园)</h3>
        <p class="text-gray-700">Shenzhen's answer to Beijing's 798 — a creative arts district with galleries, design studios, cafés, and weekend markets. Great for an afternoon wander.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Lianhua Mountain (long text → float wrap) -->
    <div class="bg-white border border-gray-200 rounded-2xl p-6 mb-6 overflow-hidden">
      <div class="float-left mr-8 mb-4 w-full md:w-80 lg:w-96 rounded-2xl overflow-hidden">
        <img src="/images/shenzhen/lianhua-mountain.png?v=3" alt="Lianhua Mountain Park panoramic view of Shenzhen skyline from summit" class="w-full h-auto object-cover" loading="lazy" />
      </div>
      <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">Lianhua Mountain Park (莲花山公园)</h3>
      <p class="text-gray-700">A hilltop park in the center of the city with panoramic views of Shenzhen's skyline. Free entry, and the hike up takes about 20 minutes. If you're here in the evening, the hilltop offers the best vantage point for the <strong>Civic Center light show (市民中心灯光秀)</strong> — a breathtaking display where dozens of skyscrapers light up in perfect sync, transforming the entire downtown skyline into a giant canvas of neon, animation, and shifting colors. Think lasers, LED grids, and futuristic visuals pulsing to music — a pure cyberpunk city spectacle that captures Shenzhen's identity as China's tech capital. Shows typically run on weekend evenings.</p>
      <div class="clear-both"></div>
    </div>

    <!-- Window of the World (short text → keep 2-col grid) -->
    <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-8 items-start bg-white border border-gray-200 rounded-2xl p-6 mb-6">
      <div class="w-full rounded-2xl overflow-hidden">
        <img src="/images/shenzhen/window-of-the-world.png" alt="Window of the World theme park miniature Eiffel Tower replica in Shenzhen" class="w-full h-auto object-cover" loading="lazy" />
      </div>
      <div>
        <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">Window of the World (世界之窗)</h3>
        <p class="text-gray-700">A theme park with miniature versions of famous landmarks from around the world. Cheesy but fun — especially the cultural shows.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Shenzhen Bay Park (long text → float wrap) -->
    <div class="bg-white border border-gray-200 rounded-2xl p-6 mb-6 overflow-hidden">
      <div class="float-left mr-8 mb-4 w-full md:w-80 lg:w-96 rounded-2xl overflow-hidden">
        <img src="/images/shenzhen/shenzhen-bay-park.png" alt="Shenzhen Bay Park coastal boardwalk sunset view across water to Hong Kong" class="w-full h-auto object-cover" loading="lazy" />
      </div>
      <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">Shenzhen Bay Park (深圳湾公园)</h3>
      <p class="text-gray-700">A 15-kilometer coastal park with views of Shenzhen Bay and Hong Kong's New Territories across the water. Perfect for sunset walks or camping. If you visit during <strong>migratory bird season (October to April, peaking December–March)</strong>, the shoreline comes alive with thousands of birds — black-faced spoonbills, red-billed gulls, and more. Early morning or late afternoon are the best times to watch them feed along the mudflats.</p>
      <div class="clear-both"></div>
    </div>

    <!-- Dameisha Beach (short text → keep 2-col grid) -->
    <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-8 items-start bg-white border border-gray-200 rounded-2xl p-6 mb-6">
      <div class="w-full rounded-2xl overflow-hidden">
        <img src="/images/shenzhen/dameisha-beach.png" alt="Dameisha Beach golden sand clear blue water popular beach in Shenzhen" class="w-full h-auto object-cover" loading="lazy" />
      </div>
      <div>
        <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">Dameisha Beach (大梅沙)</h3>
        <p class="text-gray-700">Shenzhen's most popular beach, about 30 minutes from the city center. Clean sand and swimming areas. Gets crowded on weekends.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Mountains-Sea-City Trail (long text → float wrap) -->
    <div class="bg-white border border-gray-200 rounded-2xl p-6 mb-12 overflow-hidden">
      <div class="float-left mr-8 mb-4 w-full md:w-80 lg:w-96 rounded-2xl overflow-hidden">
        <img src="/images/shenzhen/mountains-sea-city.png" alt="Mountains Sea City coastal cycling trail scenic bike path along Shenzhen coastline" class="w-full h-auto object-cover" loading="lazy" />
      </div>
      <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-3">For Outdoor & Sports Lovers — Shenzhen's "Mountains-Sea-City" Trail (山海连城)</h3>
      <p class="text-gray-700 mb-3">If you're into cycling or hiking, Shenzhen's city-wide "Mountains-Sea-City" initiative has created some fantastic outdoor routes:</p>
      <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-2 text-gray-700">
        <li><strong>Coastal Cycling (太子湾 → 深圳湾):</strong> Ride along the dedicated bike path from Taiziwan to Shenzhen Bay Park. The Taiziwan section offers a 270° panoramic sea view, with the Shenzhen Bay Bridge and Hong Kong's mountains on the horizon. For a longer ride, the full western coastal route stretches about 50 km from Xihuan Mangrove to Futian Mangrove Eco-Park — a perfect half-day cycling adventure with sea breeze all the way. Just take a shared bike and ride.</li>
        <li><strong>Mountain Hiking (七娘山):</strong> Head to Qiniangshan (七娘山), Shenzhen's second highest peak at 869 meters. Located on the Dapeng Peninsula, it's surrounded by the sea on three sides, giving you spectacular mountain-meets-ocean views at the summit. It's part of the Dapeng Peninsula National Geopark, about 1.5 hours from downtown Shenzhen.</li>
      </ul>
      <div class="clear-both"></div>
    </div>

    <h2 id="getting-around" class="text-3xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-6 mt-12">🚇 Getting Around</h2>
    <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-3 text-lg text-gray-700 mb-12">
      <li><strong>Subway:</strong> 12 lines covering the city and extending to the Hong Kong border (Luohu and Futian stations). Check the <a href="/en/transport/metro-bus/" class="text-blue-600 hover:underline">Metro & Bus Guide for Major Chinese Cities</a> for line maps.</li>
      <li><strong>Didi:</strong> Cheap and efficient. Most drivers understand basic English pick-up points. See <a href="/en/transport/didi/" class="text-blue-600 hover:underline">How to Use Didi in China as a Foreigner</a> for setup.</li>
      <li><strong>High-speed rail:</strong> Shenzhen North Station connects to Guangzhou (30 min), Hong Kong West Kowloon (15 min), and other cities. Read the <a href="/en/transport/high-speed-rail/" class="text-blue-600 hover:underline">How to Book and Ride China High-Speed Rail</a> for booking details.</li>
      <li><strong>Walking:</strong> The city center (Futian and Nanshan) is very walkable with wide sidewalks and many parks.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 id="where-to-stay" class="text-3xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-6 mt-12">🏨 Where to Stay</h2>
    <div class="bg-white border border-gray-200 rounded-2xl p-6 mb-6"><h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">Futian District (福田区) — Best for first-time visitors</h3><p class="text-gray-700">The central business district has the best metro connections and easy access to the Hong Kong border. High-end hotels and shopping malls.</p></div>
    <div class="bg-white border border-gray-200 rounded-2xl p-6 mb-6"><h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">Nanshan District (南山区) — Best for tech and coastal vibes</h3><p class="text-gray-700">Home to Shenzhen's tech headquarters and close to Shenzhen Bay. More relaxed, with great seafood restaurants.</p></div>
    <div class="bg-white border border-gray-200 rounded-2xl p-6 mb-12"><h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">Luohu District (罗湖区) — Best for budget travel</h3><p class="text-gray-700">The older center is near the Luohu border crossing to Hong Kong. More affordable hotels and the famous Dongmen shopping street.</p></div>

    <!-- ==================== WHAT TO EAT ==================== -->
    <h2 id="what-to-eat" class="text-3xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-6 mt-12">🍜 What to Eat</h2>
    <p class="text-lg leading-relaxed text-gray-700 mb-6">Shenzhen's food scene is a mix of Cantonese heritage and migrant flavors from all over China. Fresh seafood is the highlight.</p>

    <!-- Food cards with images -->
    <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-6 mb-12">
      <!-- Chaoshan Beef Hotpot -->
      <div class="bg-white border border-gray-200 rounded-2xl overflow-hidden">
        <div class="flex items-center justify-center bg-gray-50 p-3">
          <img src="/images/shenzhen/chaoshan-hotpot.png" alt="Chaoshan beef hotpot thinly sliced fresh beef in clear broth" class="max-w-full max-h-56 object-contain" loading="lazy" />
        </div>
        <div class="p-4">
          <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-gray-900 mb-1">Chaoshan Beef Hotpot (潮汕牛肉火锅)</h3>
          <p class="text-gray-600 text-base">Thinly sliced premium beef in a light broth. The beef is so fresh it's often still warm.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Cantonese Seafood -->
      <div class="bg-white border border-gray-200 rounded-2xl overflow-hidden">
        <div class="flex items-center justify-center bg-gray-50 p-3">
          <img src="/images/shenzhen/seafood.png" alt="Cantonese style seafood fresh clams shrimp crab with ginger scallion" class="max-w-full max-h-56 object-contain" loading="lazy" />
        </div>
        <div class="p-4">
          <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-gray-900 mb-1">Cantonese-Style Seafood (粤式海鲜)</h3>
          <p class="text-gray-600 text-base">Clams, shrimp, and crab prepared Cantonese-style with ginger and scallions.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Coconut Chicken -->
      <div class="bg-white border border-gray-200 rounded-2xl overflow-hidden">
        <div class="flex items-center justify-center bg-gray-50 p-3">
          <img src="/images/shenzhen/coconut-chicken.png" alt="Coconut chicken hotpot tender chicken in coconut water broth signature Shenzhen dish" class="max-w-full max-h-56 object-contain" loading="lazy" />
        </div>
        <div class="p-4">
          <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-gray-900 mb-1">Coconut Chicken (椰子鸡)</h3>
          <p class="text-gray-600 text-base">A Shenzhen-born classic: tender chicken cooked in fresh coconut water, served with a dipping sauce of chili, soy sauce, and lime.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Dongmen Snacks -->
      <div class="bg-white border border-gray-200 rounded-2xl overflow-hidden">
        <div class="flex items-center justify-center bg-gray-50 p-3">
          <img src="/images/shenzhen/dongmen-snacks.png" alt="Dongmen pedestrian street night market grilled squid skewers fruit tea stalls" class="max-w-full max-h-56 object-contain" loading="lazy" />
        </div>
        <div class="p-4">
          <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-gray-900 mb-1">Dongmen Snacks (东门小吃)</h3>
          <p class="text-gray-600 text-base">The Dongmen pedestrian street is packed with stalls selling everything from grilled squid to fruit tea.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="not-prose mt-16">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-900 mb-8">📚 Related Guides</h2>
      <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-4">
        <a href="/en/cities/city-select/" class="block bg-white border border-gray-200 rounded-2xl p-6 hover:shadow-lg hover:border-blue-300 transition">🗺️ <strong>How Many Days in China?</strong> — Plan your full itinerary</a>
        <a href="/en/cities/guangzhou-guide/" class="block bg-white border border-gray-200 rounded-2xl p-6 hover:shadow-lg hover:border-blue-300 transition">🥟 <strong>Guangzhou Travel Guide</strong> — Just 30 minutes by rail</a>
        <a href="/en/visa/visa/transit-240/" class="block bg-white border border-gray-200 rounded-2xl p-6 hover:shadow-lg hover:border-blue-300 transition">🛂 <strong>China 240-Hour Visa-Free Transit Explained</strong> — Visa rules for transit travelers</a>
        <a href="/en/transport/transport-guide/" class="block bg-white border border-gray-200 rounded-2xl p-6 hover:shadow-lg hover:border-blue-300 transition">🚄 <strong>How to Get Around China</strong> — All your options</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </article>
</Layout>
